\# This is a comment

\# Style as normal
.PRINTSTYLE TYPESET
\# Style as typewritten, double-spaced
\# .PRINTSTYLE TYPEWRITE

.START

.TITLE "The mom Tutorial"
The macro package for groff called mom is primarily used to generate PDF and PostScript files.

\# Number variable that is incremented by 3
.nr age 29 3
\# String variable
.ds name Ludvig Westerdahl

Hello \*[name]! You are \n[age] years old.

\# Increments the variable keeps the state.
\n+[age] is \n[age] which is greater than \n-[age].

\# Manipulating the number variable
.nr age 5
The age is now \n[age].

.nr age +13
But we can increase it to \n[age].

\# We can even break up longer macros using \<CR>, but
\# be careful for numeric expressions since the spaces otherwise
\# would result in multiple arguments to the macro .nr
.nr age \
    ( \
    \n+[age]*0 \
    + \
    \n+[age] \
    )
And then incrementing twice it to \n[age] respecting the variables increment using the trick of multiplying by zero.

.QUOTE
This is how we write quotes. To toggle it off, give the .QUOTE macro any argument.
In this example we gave it OFF, but we could have used any other non-empty string.
.QUOTE OFF

\# next up: https://www.schaffter.ca/mom/momdoc/typesetting.html#top

